  "term": "REM Sleep Behavior Disorder",
  "definition": "REM sleep behavior disorder is a condition in which a person shows vigorous, sometimes violent movement during REM sleep and can be hard to wake. After an episode, the person often vividly remembers a dream that matches the aggressive behavior, and the episodes can lead to injury to the person or others.",
